# GPUI Visual Test Screenshot

Window: 

This file marks the attempt to capture the window using GPUI's
screen capture infrastructure.

For full pixel-level capture, the TestScreenCaptureSource implementation
would need to be extended to:

1. Capture the GPUI window's rendered frame using platform GPU read-back
2. Convert the captured frame to RGB/BGRA pixel data
3. Provide the pixel data through the screen capture stream callback

The GPUI test framework provides VisualTestContext for interaction testing
(mouse clicks, keyboard, state verification). Visual regression testing
can be built on top by capturing and comparing pixel data between runs.
